      "kind": "parser_admitted"
    },
    {
      "file": "glib/guri.c",
      "function": "uri_cleanup",
      "line": 603,
      "code": "g_string_append (copy, \"%20\");",
      "note": "First project-side input consumption on the crashing path that creates vulnerability-relevant state: `uri_cleanup()` rewrites the attacker's literal space inside the bracketed host into `%20`, introducing the `%` later treated as a zone-ID delimiter.",
      "kind": "source"
    },
    {
      "file": "glib/guri.c",
      "function": "parse_host",
      "line": null,
      "code": "pct = strchr (addr, '%');\nif (pct)\n  *pct = '\\0';",
      "note": "The fix patch replaces this ad hoc handling with `parse_ip_literal()` plus `uri_decode()` on a separately split zone substring. That patch alignment is static only: Stage 01 reproduced the vulnerable build but did not execute the fixed build.",
      "kind": "root_cause_function"
    },
    {
      "file": "glib/guri.c",
      "function": "parse_host",
      "line": 408,
      "code": "pct = strchr (addr, '%');\nif (pct)\n  *pct = '\\0';",
