    {
      "file": "glib/gstring.c",
      "function": "g_string_insert_len",
      "line": null,
      "code": "memcpy (string->str + pos_unsigned, val, len_unsigned);",
      "note": "The saved sanitizer trace reports `READ of size 5` at this line and shows the call chain `g_string_append_uri_escaped() -> _uri_encoder() -> g_string_append_len() -> g_string_insert_len()`. Step 13 fixes that copy length at 5 from `g_utf8_skip[0xF8]`, so this `memcpy` reads 5 bytes starting at the trailing `0xF8` in the 6-byte region allocated in `parse_host()` at `glib/guri.c:405`; ASan reports the first invalid byte immediately to the right of that region.",
      "kind": "sink_function"
    },
